  "worked_solution": "Our tangent line approximation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =4x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $y(\\frac{3}{2})$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{3}{2}) & \u2248L(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})-2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
